# Semantic HTML

## Interactive Elements
- URL change → `<a href="...">`
- Action → `<button type="button">` or `<button type="submit">`
- Never `<div>`/`<span>` with click handlers

**Button types (always specify):**
- `type="submit"` — submits form
- `type="button"` — no form behavior (default for most buttons)
- `type="reset"` — resets form

## Page Structure
**Required landmarks:**
- `<header>` — site header
- `<main>` — one per page, primary content
- `<footer>` — site footer

**Use semantic elements for:**
- `<nav>` — navigation sections
- `<aside>` — supplementary content
- `<section>` — page sections with headings
- `<article>` — self-contained, syndicatable content (blog posts, comments)

**Use `<div>` for:** layout containers, styling hooks, visual grouping

## Headings
- One `<h1>` per page
- Sequential hierarchy (don't skip levels going down)
- Every `<section>` should have a heading

## Lists
Use `<ul>`/`<ol>` for related item collections (nav links, feature grids, menus) even if styled inline. Use `list-none` to remove bullets.

## Forms
- Labels required: `<label for="id">` or wrap input in `<label>`
- Use semantic input types: `email`, `tel`, `url`, `search`, `date`
- Use validation attributes: `required`, `minlength`, `maxlength`, `min`, `max`

## Images
- Content images: descriptive `alt` text
- Decorative images: empty `alt=""`

## Accessibility
- Prefer native elements (`<button>`, `<a>`, `<input>`) — built-in keyboard/screen reader support
- ARIA only for: icon-only buttons (`aria-label`), status updates (`aria-live`), custom widgets
- Don't duplicate: `<button role="button">` ✗ | `<button aria-label="Save">Save</button>` ✗
- Preserve focus visibility: use `focus-visible:ring-2`, never `outline-none`

## Patterns
```html
<!-- Modal -->
<dialog>
  <h2>Title</h2>
  <button type="button">Close</button>
</dialog>

<!-- Loading state -->
<div aria-live="polite" aria-busy="true">Loading...</div>
```

---

**Core principle**: Use semantic HTML — it's accessible by default. Use `<div>` for layout and styling, semantic elements for meaning.
